    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "A cinema sells 120 tickets for a total of $\\$1535$. Each child ticket costs $\\$10.50$ and each adult ticket costs $\\$16$. How many child and how many adult tickets are sold?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "70 child tickets and 50 adult tickets.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the number of child tickets and $y$ the number of adult tickets.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+y&=120 &&(1)\\\\10.50x+16y&=1535 &&(2)\\\\10.50x+10.50y&=1260 &&10.50\\times(1)\\\\5.50y&=275 &&(2)-10.50\\times(1)\\\\y&=50\\\\x&=120-50\\\\x&=70\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, 70 child tickets and 50 adult tickets are sold.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
